    "answer": "to{} see-someone-off-(at-a-station,-an-airport,-etc.)/escort-(e.g.-home) | follow-something-with-one's-eyes-until-it-is-out-of-sight | let-pass/pass-up-(an-opportunity-etc.)/let-a-pitch-go-by-(baseball)/watch-a-batted-ball-go-into-the-stands | shelve-(a-plan,-deliberation-on-a-bill,-etc.)/postpone | have-someone-related-or-close-to-you-die/bury-someone | take-care-of-somebody-until-he-dies | wait-and-see/continue-(e.g.-in-legal-contexts)",
    "mnemonic": "You know the words <ja>見る</ja> and <ja>送る</ja> by now, hopefully. Here you're \"seeing\" the \"sending.\" You're seeing someone off, so this verb is <vocabulary>to see off</vocabulary>. This can also mean <vocabulary>to put off</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>to pass on</vocabulary>, since it's as though you're just passively seeing someone (or something) off rather than taking action and going with them.",
